From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:42:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: allow a CSID without a same-index VFE

Since the VFE get/put special case was removed, every CSID powers the
VFE with its own index before switching on. MSM8916, MSM8226, MSM8939 and
MSM8953 have more CSIDs than VFEs and route every CSID through ISPIF, so
on those SoCs CSID1 and above first indexed past the VFE array and, after
the parent device ops were introduced, failed to power on with -EINVAL.
A sensor connected through CSID1 therefore cannot stream.

The ordering is only needed from SDM845 onwards. When ISPIF is present
and no VFE has the CSID's index, power the CSID without a parent.

This change was developed with an AI coding assistant, which traced the
power path and wrote the patch; it was build-tested for ARM with the
MSM8226 configuration. It has not yet been tested on hardware with a
sensor routed through CSID1.

Fixes: b2c2715e5aaf ("media: qcom: camss: Remove special case for VFE get/put")
Fixes: b1e6eef535df ("media: qcom: camss: Decouple VFE from CSID")
Assisted-by: LLM [tools]
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 17 +++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index df8af4923..bc2d94b64 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -3643,17 +3643,18 @@ void camss_pm_domain_off(struct camss *camss, int id)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A CSID powers the VFE with the same index first, which SDM845 and later
+ * require. SoCs such as MSM8916 and MSM8226 have more CSIDs than VFEs and
+ * route every CSID through ISPIF, so a CSID without a same-index VFE has no
+ * parent to power.
+ */
 static int vfe_parent_dev_ops_get(struct camss *camss, int id)
 {
-	int ret = -EINVAL;
-
-	if (id < camss->res->vfe_num) {
-		struct vfe_device *vfe = &camss->vfe[id];
-
-		ret = vfe_get(vfe);
-	}
+	if (id >= camss->res->vfe_num)
+		return camss->ispif ? 0 : -EINVAL;
 
-	return ret;
+	return vfe_get(&camss->vfe[id]);
 }
 
 static int vfe_parent_dev_ops_put(struct camss *camss, int id)
